    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1106">

                <pb facs="1075" n="909" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg909"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/20586</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Edwards to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-28T20:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Murguia officially states Villa is eliminated and only police work
                    remains to be done. That Villa’s physical condition has forced his retirement is
                    quite beyond doubt. Through trains to and from <pb facs="1076" n="910"
                        xml:id="pg910"/> Mexico City are now inaugurated by the National Line. Food
                    shipments to the south from this point are daily increasing and the outgoing
                    number of Mexicans has become an exodus. That there is to be a state of
                    tranquillity is general opinion with them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
